                <pb facs="0223" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 1/1793: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Haskell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-08T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1923—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Congressman Porter:</p>
                <p>I am much gratified by the results reported in your telegram of June 6, 5
                    p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
